From 63b7115e964e4bd317a92b29b422237a842bd76d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:27:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] backend: Adds support for
 wlr-output-power-management-unstable-v1 protocol.

Creates the output power manager and handles `set_mode` by disabling,
resp. enabling the output through wlr_output_state. The output remains
in the output layout while powered off, so windows stay where they are.
Outputs that are not in the layout (eg. disabled through configuration)
are left untouched.

wlroots' wlr_output_power_management_v1.h includes the protocol's server
header, so the protocol XML from wlr-protocols is added to third_party/
and the header generated along with the other protocol headers.

Permits DPMS from clients, eg. `wlopm` run from `swayidle`.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
